title: SSH Client Connecting to Reverse Proxy Tunneling
status: experimental
description: Detects ssh.exe executed with the -R option, which creates a reverse port forward from a remote server back to the internal network. Attackers use this to expose internal services such as RDP to an external host and bypass firewall restrictions. Observed in the Akira intrusion on domain controllers and servers.
references:
    - https://thedfirreport.com/2026/06/29/from-bing-search-to-ransomware-bumblebee-and-adaptixc2-deliver-akira-3/
author: Sümeyra Yüksel
date: 2026/10/20
tags:
    - attack.command-and-control
    - attack.t1572
    - attack.t1090
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_img:
        - Image|endswith: '\ssh.exe'
        - OriginalFileName: 'ssh.exe'
    selection_cli:
        CommandLine|contains: ' -R'
    condition: all of selection_*
fields:
    - Image
    - User
    - SourceIp
    - DestinationIp
    - DestinationPort
level: high
